1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Dembaş temaşevanên me yên hêja, temaşevanên me yên ezîz.
 
Good day our esteemed viewers, our dear viewers.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Em hêvîdar in hûn hemî di nav xêr û xweşiyê da bin.
 
We hope you are all well and in good health.

3
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Em niha li mafreqê gundê Be'dîna ne, bi rastî em ê herin û
derbasî gundê Be'dîna bibin.
 
We are currently at the crossroads of Be'dîna village, we
are going to go and enter Be'dîna village.

4
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Gundê min, silavên min ji hemî kesên ji gundê Be'dîna ra.
 
My village, my greetings to everyone from Be'dîna village.

5
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Silavên min ji miletê Kurd tevahî ra heye.
 
My greetings to the entire Kurdish nation.

6
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Lê ji gundê Be'dîna jî bi taybet em ê derbasî malbetekê
bibin, ew malbet jî navê wan Ehmedî Tenbel.
 
But specifically from Be'dîna village, we will visit a
family, that family is named Ehmedî Tenbel.

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Silavên min ji wê malbetê ra jî heye.
 
My greetings to that family as well.

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Gava em bifikirin beriya pêncî şêst salî da, li her gundekî
çar pênc mal,
 
When we think back fifty, sixty years, in every village four
or five families,

9
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:03,000
bi vî karî radibûn, karê Sinciq.
 
would do this work, the work of Sinciq (Fruit
leather/Pestil).

10
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Lê niha mixabin em nabînin, ev tişt jî kêm kêm tê çêkirin.
 
But now unfortunately we don't see it, this thing is rarely
made.

11
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Lê xalê Ehmed ji pêncî şêst salî da, ev kar ji bav û kalê
xwe ra kir. Lê niha hîn bi vî karî radibe.
 
But uncle Ehmed has been doing this work inherited from his
ancestors for fifty, sixty years. And he is still doing this
work now.

12
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Karê Sinciq... wek em zanin, hefteyê çûyî me tirî ji we ra
sawirand, niha mewsima tirî ye.
 
The work of Sinciq... as we know, last week we filmed grapes
for you, now is the grape season.

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Xalê Ehmed jî piştî tirî, wî diqutê, dimis, hinek dimis
çêdikin,
 
Uncle Ehmed too, after the grapes, he crushes them, grape
molasses, some make grape molasses,

14
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
û hinek ji dimis jî sinciq tê çêkirin.
 
and some of the grape molasses is used to make Sinciq.

15
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Bi rastî berê, navçeya Raco, hemî gundên navçeya Raco bi vî
karî radibûn, û li her gundekî şeş heft mal bi vî karî
radibûn.
 
Actually in the past, the Raco district, all the villages in
Raco district used to do this work, and in every village six
or seven families used to do this work.

16
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Lê niha jî em vî tiştî nabînin. Ji wê me'neyê jî me xwest em
derbasî gundê Be'dîna bibin, û ji gundê Be'dîna jî em
derbasî mala xalê Ehmed bibin.
 
But now we don't see this thing. For that reason we wanted
to visit Be'dîna village, and in Be'dîna village we wanted
to visit uncle Ehmed's house.

17
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Em bisawirînin, em bi hev ra nas bikin, çawa sinciq tê
çêkirin.
 
So we can film, so we can learn together, how sinciq is
made.

18
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Hemî reqemê xalê Ehmed didim vira, kesên dixwazin dilê wan
bi sinciq daxwaze, dikarin lê bigerin û jê ra bêjin "çi
giringiya wê hebe, ji me ra bişîne".
 
I will provide all of uncle Ehmed's numbers here, people who
want, who have a craving for sinciq, can call him and say
"whatever it costs, send some for us".

19
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Hinek sinciq, hinek dimisê şîrîn...
 
Some sinciq, some sweet grape molasses...

20
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Bi me ra bin em ê herin vîdyoyê da nas bikin, çawa sinciq li
Be'dîna tê çêkirin, û bi taybet jî li cem xalê Ehmed.
 
Stay with us, we will go and see in the video how sinciq is
made in Be'dîna, and specifically at uncle Ehmed's place.

21
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Belê temaşevanên me yên hêja, destpêkê vîdyoyê da min ji we
ra xeber da bû.
 
Yes our esteemed viewers, at the beginning of the video I
told you.

22
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Ez ê derbasî gundê Be'dîna bibim û ji gundê Be'dîna jî ez ê
derbasî malbetekê bibim,
 
I will go to Be'dîna village and from Be'dîna village I will
visit a family,

23
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:07,000
Niha jî em derbasî cem xalê Ehmed bûn, em ê bi hev ra nas
bikin çawa dimisê reza tê çêkirin, û çawa sinciq li vira tê
çêkirin.
 
Now we have visited uncle Ehmed's place, we will learn
together how grape molasses is made, and how sinciq is made
here.

24
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Merheba xalo.
 
Hello uncle.

25
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Ehlen, ehlen û sehlen bik.
 
Welcome, welcome to you.

26
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Tu çawa yî xalê Ehmed?
 
How are you uncle Ehmed?

27
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Welle elhemdilillah rehetiye, tu çawa yî?
 
By God, thank God it's peaceful, how are you?

28
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Saxî ya te. Berî giya, em sipasiya te dikin jiber ku te
deriyê xwe ji me ra vekir.
 
Your health. First of all, we thank you for opening your
door to us.

29
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Em bi van îro, li cem te... ez û kamêra xwe ve herin, me
xwest em derbasî cem te bin.
 
Today, with this, at your place... me and my camera will go,
we wanted to visit you.

30
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Destê te diêşin, sax bî, ser çavan, keremkin.
 
Let your hands not hurt, may you be healthy, you are
welcome, go ahead.

31
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Sax bî, ser çavan.
 
May you be healthy, you are welcome.

32
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Min ji te, navê te... navê te Ahmed, Xelîl e, malbat
"Tenbel" dizanin. Ehmedê Xelîl, tenbel nîne...
 
I, from you, your name... your name is Ahmed, Xelîl, the
family is known as "Tenbel". Ehmedê Xelîl, he is not lazy...

33
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Û kinyeya me jî Ebdê ye.
 
And our surname is Ebdê.

34
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Bes gundiyan digotin Tenbel, tenbela tê gotinê, nav...
 
But the villagers used to say Tenbel, tenbela is said,
name...

35
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Ev, em dikarin bibêjin kinyeya we Ebdê ye lê navê, weke
leqebek lê hatibû.
 
This, we can say your surname is Ebdê, but the name, it came
as a nickname.

36
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Leqeb bû.
 
It was a nickname.

37
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Leqebek bû. Belê.
 
It was a nickname. Yes.

38
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Xalê Ehmed, em sipasiya te dikin, em dixwazin hinekî ji me
ra xeberdî ser sinciq,
 
Uncle Ehmed, we thank you, we want you to talk to us a bit
about sinciq,

39
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:55,000
destpêkê, çawa hûn pê radibin, çawa çêdibe heya taliyê, heya
ku cehêz dibe.
 
from the beginning, how you start it, how it's made until
the end, until it's ready.

40
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Û em dibînin niha tu dimis jî çêdikî. Em dixwazin hinekî ji
me ra xeber dî.
 
And we see now you are making molasses too. We want you to
tell us a little about it.

41
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Temam... Ew ewilî sinciq... bi xwe em çaxê guza yan tiştê
din em dixin navê... em dişoxulin.
 
Okay... First, sinciq... we ourselves, when we add walnuts
or other things inside it... we process it.

42
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Em bînin darê... tirî yê... şêrîn dibe, em dişoxilîn. Em
guza tînin, dişikînin... paşê darik dixe... me re... pê ve
dikin...
 
We bring the wood... the grapes... it becomes sweet, we
process it. We bring walnuts, break them... then put them on
sticks... with us... attach them...

43
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:20,000
... bi derziya... em pê ve dikin...
 
... with a needle... we attach them...

44
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:27,000
û em bi darika girê didin. Piştî girêdanê em derîn tirî
tînin... meser kêlê ka em diçilqînin, em dikin şerbet.
 
and we tie them to the sticks. After tying, we bring
grapes... near the press we crush them, we make sherbet
(grape juice).

45
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:36,000
dixe helê, vira... yek, du, sê... sê helê me hene. Yekî
şerbete em dirijînin, boş dikin...
 
put it in the vat, here... one, two, three... we have three
vats. One for the sherbet, we pour it, empty it...

46
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:40,000
ewa... dikele, em boş dikin ta çaran... ta kelandinê xirav
dibe...
 
that one... boils, we empty it into four... until the
boiling reduces...

47
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:47,000
em boş dikin wî dinê... di wî da, disafe. Disafe, saetekê
dimîne... û em diqulibînin, birûşk din.
 
we empty it into the other... in that one, it settles. It
settles, stays for an hour... and we turn it over, strain
it.

48
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Em vî dinê, taştî palulê.
 
We put it in this other one, the bowl for the pelûl
(pudding-like mixture).

49
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:55,000
Em dikarin bibêjin, destpêkê tirî tê derket, şîrîn bûye...
hîn berî ku tirî xwe tînin... dicilvînin. Piştî wê hîn
dikelînin.
 
We can say, initially the grapes come out, they become
sweet... even before bringing the grapes themselves... they
crush them. After that they boil them.

50
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Çima?
 
Why?

51
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Em dikarin bibêjin, çend kes jî hene... niha em dibînin ey
guze lê be'îva ye.
 
We can say, there are several people too... now we see these
are walnuts but with almonds.

52
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Ê guz e, ev.
 
These are walnuts.

53
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Ê be'îv jî hene.
 
There are almonds too.

54
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Ê be'îv jî hene... çend salin, hûn bi vî karî radibin.
 
There are almonds too... how many years have you been doing
this work?

55
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Ev karo... tiştê kê hînî. Welle ev kar... ji berê da, kalikê
me digotin Evdê Tenbel, wî kar dikir.
 
This work... how did you learn it? By God this work... since
the past, our grandfather called Evdê Tenbel, he used to do
this work.

56
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:22,000
Mehmedê kalko, rehmetiyê bavê min... van hemûya, yê esasî
dişixulin... digotin calko...
 
Grandfather Mehmed, my late father... all of them, the main
ones worked... they called him grandfather...

57
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:28,000
belkî tu jî dizanî. Wê paşê, apê me Heno, rehmetî, wî
tenbel, Miştexî Hemko, giya ev ne, giya koro giya ye... jê
berê. Em jî yên ku...
 
maybe you know too. Then later, our uncle Heno, the late,
that Tenbel, Mistefa Hemko, all these, it's all their
work... from before. We too, the ones who...

58
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Em dikarin bibêjin ev kar we ji bav û kalê xwe da
wergirtiye, me jî ji kalikê xwe da hilgirtiye.
 
We can say you inherited this work from your ancestors, we
took it from our grandfather too.

59
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Digotin xeliyê tembel, meselen... û em piçûk bûn, em bi van
ra, şixulin, me jî ev kar ji bav û kalê xwe ra hilgirtiye.
 
They used to say Xelîl Tenbel, for example... and we were
small, we worked with them, we also took this work from our
ancestors.

60
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:44,000
Em niha dibînin, em dikarin bibêjin... nêzîkî sed salî ye ev
kar heye. Û li her gundekî çar pênc malbat bi vî karî
radibûn.
 
We see now, we can say... this work has existed for nearly a
hundred years. And in every village four or five families
used to do this work.

61
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:47,000
Çima?
 
Why?

62
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:50,000
Ji yek... niha em dibînin li gundê Be'dîna, bes tenê niha
hûn mane.
 
From one... now we see in Be'dîna village, only you are left
now.

63
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Noko ez im, kes naşixule. Ew berê, siyek hebûn, li Helebê
bûn...
 
Now it's me, no one else works. Back then, there were shade
places, they were in Aleppo...

64
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:58,000
em bîst pênc mal dişuxulîn. Ê noko kes naşuxule, xêncî min
kes naşuxule.
 
we, twenty-five families, used to work. And now no one
works, except me, no one works.

65
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Sebeb çi ye niha, em dibînin pir kes bi vî karî ranabin...
karekî zehmet e, zehmetiya wê pir e. Lê di xwe ra nakin, em
dikarin bibêjin?
 
What is the reason now, we see many people don't do this
work... is it a difficult work, is its difficulty too much?
They don't bother, can we say?

66
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:14,000
Welle cehfa wê jî pir e, wekî berê, me derber şuxulên li
Helebê hebû, noka kêm bûye. Ji wî derî, em difiroşin.
 
By God, its effort is a lot too, like before, we used to
sell the products in Aleppo, now it has decreased. From that
place, we sell.

67
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:22,000
Niha mesela em dikarin bibêjin zirbûnê te hene, bi vî
sinciqê çêdikin, yan dixe binê xwe ra...
 
Now for example we can say you have customers, who make this
sinciq, or it is requested from you...

68
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Çima, çend zibûn me hene? Cîh cih me hene, em... gava meriv
dibêje ji me ra bixebitînin, em ji gendî ya re çêdikin...
 
Why, how many customers do we have? We have them in places,
we... when someone says make it for us, we make it for the
villages...

69
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
Dimisê me jî, em didinê û sunciqa jî em didinê.
 
Our grape molasses too, we give it, and the sinciq too, we
give it.

70
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,000
Em dikarin bibêjin her sal jî hûn bi vî karî radibin. Tevî
karî dikî.
 
We can say you do this work every year. You do all the work.

71
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:38,000
Her sal, çima na... her sal me wekî ev karê xwe dişixulin.
 
Every year, why not... every year we work like this.

72
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Ez dixwazim, te ji me ra xeber da... çi qas wext gerek e
gava hûn vî sinciqê diçêkin, ta hûn derdixin...
 
I want, you told us... how much time is needed when you make
this sinciq, until you take it out...

73
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:54,000
Ev sunciqo, bi xwe gava me ne ew bi dar xist, çar şevan bi
camên xwe, evên roj lê dixin ne, şevan rûniştin ne.
 
This sinciq, when we put it on sticks, four nights outside,
those hit by the sun, they sit at night.

74
00:07:54,000 --> 00:08:00,000
Ev na, çarê... çaran şevan bi cemed ne, deh roj, temam dibe.
Gava deh roj tê da kirin, xwe, quretiyê bû.
 
This no, four... four nights with the cold, ten days, it's
done. When ten days pass, it dried, it hardened.

75
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,000
Ew taqê lê kî... yekî carî derdixin, jiber ku hişk bibe.
 
That layer on it... you take it out once, so it becomes dry.

76
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:09,000
Li derî ber rojê ye. Em radixin heta roj lê dixin... Ku hişk
bibin, heta rojê dikin.
 
Outside under the sun. We lay it out until the sun hits
it... When they get dry, we put them under the sun.

77
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:18,000
Û ro bi ro jî em dibînin te pelûlek çêkirine... pelûl pê ve
çêkin, çêdibin?
 
And day by day too we see you made a pelûl... you make pelûl
with it, is it possible?

78
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:38,000
Çima? Pelûl, yekî, a cer, a cer çêdibin. Belê.
 
Why? Pelûl, one, clay, in clay it is made. Yes.

79
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Niha ev tiriyê hîn nû ye. Ew tirî me da, wî çilqale ye,
şûşê.
 
Now these grapes are still new. Those grapes we gave, they
are in the press, glass.

80
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:52,000
Her tirî dibe dimis, lê... bes navê yek mu'eyen e...
 
Every grape becomes molasses, but... only the name of one is
specific...

81
00:08:52,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Na bê... mu'eyen e, eva yê dikulgane. Ev tiriyê dibe, ev...
dimis û sinciq. Û şerbetê xwo pak, têt derê...
 
No... it's specific, this is the dikulgan grape. This grape
makes, this... molasses and sinciq. And its sherbet is pure,
it comes out...

82
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Belê. Tê, tê... ev nû gîhandine, ne xereq e. Na xereqe... no
ka ev bi niya, reşe ki, xel be, evo be, şerbete gedê na
wakibê.
 
Yes. It comes, it comes... this is freshly ripened, not
spoiled. Not spoiled... now this one here, it's black, if
it's soil, this one, its sherbet won't be like that.

83
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:17,000
Ewa şerbeta wî pak têt dar.
 
That one, its sherbet comes out pure.

84
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:21,000
Em dibînin ev tiriyê bes ê dimis e û pelûl e? Ev tirî...
dibe mîj... xalê Ehmed?
 
We see this grape is only for molasses and pelûl? Does this
grape... become raisins... uncle Ehmed?

85
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:29,000
Nabe mîj. Nabe mîj... Ew mîj e, jê... ê mîjî ew... ji bo mîj
e, yê... yê... a xasiyetî, mîj, ew ê hûdî ye. Ev... tîpê
hevidiyê... ev, mîj e. Ev e. Rêsî.
 
It doesn't become raisins. It doesn't become raisins... That
is raisins, from it... the one for raisins that... is for
raisins, the... the... the special one, raisins, that is the
Hêvîdî one. This... Hêvîdî type... this, is raisins. This
is. Rêsî.

86
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:34,000
Nîho em devînin te tirî hîna... li vî derî tirî na tê
şûştin, perê we ra cevlana...
 
Now we see you still have grapes... in this place the grapes
are not washed, before you press...

87
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:47,000
Na, na tê şûştin... şûştina xwa di kavê, ew na ew, di
safê... em wir da dîcivlînin, dika bî wi derî... di warda di
kelê, di warda di safê. Di safî şerbet wa kî, çovî xe zê
zînît dar xû.
 
No, they are not washed... its washing happens, that no
that, in the settling... we press it there, it goes to that
place... in there it boils, in there it settles. In the
settling, the sherbet becomes like, you put a stick in it,
you see the bottom of it.

88
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:59,000
Ew çi ya, ser bê me ra xaber de... Ev o çi ye, şe'da ye, ev
o şe'da ye... Çê pê, ayi di kavî... heno va dîdan, meselen
şerbet te da dê.
 
What is that, tell us about it... What is this, it's earth
(white soil), this is earth... What is it for, it goes in...
for example it is put in, so the sherbet comes out in it.

89
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Ev o devê pek dêd...
 
This becomes clean...

90
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Ew e ku ji te re... diguviştin fêk da, fêk tiştî pê naynin
lê.
 
That is... they squeeze it in the sack, they don't do it
with a sack anymore though.

91
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Berî... ev ya berî bi sed salî ye.
 
Before... this is from a hundred years ago.

92
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Erê, ev a kevin dar e. Berî vê belkî dused sal e.
 
Yes, this one is an old wooden one. It's maybe from two
hundred years ago.

93
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:14,000
Û ev a... ev gundê qeda, ehbab kî da hîna... ji wan anî
ya...
 
And this... this is from the village of Qada, a friend gave
it to someone... and I brought it from them...

94
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:19,000
Naha em bên Xalê Ehmed di derket... çûyîna we re...
 
Now let's come to Uncle Ahmed's passing... your process...

95
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:23,000
Çima em balê xwe didinê... axa spî lê kirine.
 
Why do we pay attention to it... they have put white earth
in it.

96
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:27,000
Axa spî ha wa ye, gava neyê kirin, jê venaqete.
 
White earth is like this, if it's not added, it won't
separate.

97
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Şerbet... î ku bê axa spî be, wek ava herimî ye.
 
The juice... if it doesn't have white earth, it's like
spoiled water.

98
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Heta naha tu... axa spî jê venaqete.
 
Until now... the white earth won't separate from it.

99
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:37,000
Dêl e (di ser de) şerbet av jê venaqete.
 
In it... the juice doesn't separate from the water.

100
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Dêl e jê venaqete lê. Tevlihev nakin, ax, şerbet jê
venaqete.
 
It doesn't separate from it. If they aren't mixed, the
earth, the juice won't separate.

101
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:46,000
Kemiya (mîqtara) çiqas her... em bên, çuwalî we re naha jê
tê... çiqas ax tê da hebe.
 
The amount of how much... let's say, your sack now gives...
how much earth should be in it.

102
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:50,000
Her kefa gindor e.. Her çuwalekî... zerikekî wusa tê keve.
 
For each handful of the round one.. For each sack... a pinch
like this is added.

103
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Zerikek, çuçik... ev o tê keve. Belê.
 
A pinch, a little bit... this is added. Yes.

104
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:59,000
Ku ev neyê kirinê, pak nabe. Ti car jê venaqete. Belê.
 
If this isn't added, it doesn't become clean. It will never
separate. Yes.

105
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Piştî hat guviştin, ev şerbeto jî tê li vê derê e ne?
 
After it's squeezed, this juice also comes here, right?

106
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:08,000
Li vê derê... boşt e ku... di vê derê ha wa, ev e ku
bikelihe.
 
Here... it is poured... in here like this, for it to boil.

107
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Ev ê ku naha tê kelandin. Em kefa mirî gî ser ra bigirin,
saetekî..
 
This is what is boiling now. We will skim off all the dead
foam from the top, for an hour..

108
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:17,000
saetek e, saet nîvekê, berxwede (diqede). Kî (ku) wekê pak
bibe...
 
for an hour, or an hour and a half, it's done. Once it
becomes clean like this...

109
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Û hileyê lê keve (pak bibe) û em ê vala kin vê derê... Dîwar
(derwê) da jî ew e bisife.
 
And it becomes pure, we empty it here... It is filtered
outside too.

110
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Ta ku ra... em ê biqulibînin, ew ê bibe dimis wisa, ne?
 
Until... we flip it, it becomes molasses like that, right?

111
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:27,000
Lê pelûl çawa tê çêkirin? Pelûla sûncik.
 
But how is the pelûl (thickened grape juice) made? The pelûl
for the sucuk.

112
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Pelûla sûncik, ji wê şerbete... derva em ku bisifînin..
 
The pelûl for the sucuk, from that grape juice... outside,
we filter it...

113
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Ew e di keve vê hilê(xulê).. ev xul e(pot). Dikeve vî çi vê
xulê.. sek (mêze) î çi bigre wa ra, ha..
 
It goes into this copper pot.. this pot. It goes into this
copper pot.. look here..

114
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Am şerbetê dikin vî xulê.. û am ê bikêlînin.
 
We put the juice in this pot... and we boil it.

115
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:46,000
Ku kel ket... nîşê... turiyê nîşê lê keve, nîşe tê dikeve
yê.
 
When it boils... the starch... a bag of starch goes into it,
the starch is added to it.

116
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Berî giya em şerbetê xwu dikin vir arê (agirê) xwe vê
dixin...
 
First, we put our juice in here and light our fire...

117
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:53,000
Piştî ev şerbet o hat kelandin em nîşe kî tekin (berdin) e..
 
after this juice is boiled, we pour the starch in it..

118
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:57,000
Em ê arî xwa bikujin wek naha te teneke çêkirî bê ne.
 
We extinguish our fire, like how you made the can earlier,
right.

119
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Em ê orî xwê bikujin û nîşê xwa yînin... em sê mer in ser
dest bikin am berdinê.
 
We extinguish our fire and bring our starch... three of us
will handle it and pour it in.

120
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:07,000
Yek mesela... tef(tev) dide... yek jî bi hêle kî da gre yê..
(diqulibîne) yê jî vala dike.
 
For example, one stirs... another turns it from one side..
and another empties it.

121
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:10,000
Saetekê, an nîvsaetekê em tev didin de biye(diqede).
 
For an hour, or an hour and a half we stir it and it's done.

122
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Piştî we pelûl teyar(amade) xwe kir ji..
 
After you have prepared your pelûl...

123
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:16,000
Em kînen vê şibekî.. we radikin û pelûl di xin? (pelûl
radixin?)
 
We bring this grate... you lift it and lay out the pelûl?

124
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:22,000
Badi (piştî) me kir pelûl, xelas em ê agirê xwa de kûjin e..
am in a. sa naxliy on ên de yê dî ya di bin. (Mesele
naqiliyên van tên, dîdane, da dibin).
 
After we make the pelûl, that's it, we extinguish our
fire... these carriers come, we put it in them and take it
away.

125
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:28,000
Am ona(wan) dibin tê da dikin vê derê ha.. mesel ê ev ha
pelûle kî tê de bi(be).
 
We bring them and put it inside this here.. for example,
some pelûl is in it.

126
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Wa ye anî(wisa hûn) tê da dikin û anî bane disekine
ava(wisa)...
 
You put it inside like this, and it stays on it like this...

127
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Heta diderve (derdikeve). Ku dervi, em kê.. bi şunê bera
(diran).
 
Until it is taken out. When it is out, we will put it on the
ropes outside.

128
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Tag r(Hêdî) em ê de xînin (bînin) vê ra wern e. belê.
 
Slowly we will bring it down here. Yes.

129
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
E va cî di hara(darê) yk di ça. (Ev a yek diçe ser darê)
 
This one goes on the wood, each one.

130
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Dara ew e am kî bên ev sûnciko hazir di be..
 
When it comes to the wood, this sucuk gets ready...

131
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Her kîlo bi çend neho ti firotin nava sûkê bi şiklê giştî am
bên bikin... da te defa frotî vî yeke?
 
How much does each kilo sell for now in the market in
general, let's say... have you sold any of this yet?

132
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,000
Welle me defa nifrotiye. Bes bikî kîçî (belkî çend) be ew,
ez nizam..
 
Well, we haven't sold it yet. But as for how much it will
be, I don't know...

133
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:02,000
Gerek dorê deh, didwazde dolar be, kîlo.
 
It should be around ten or twelve dollars a kilo.

134
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Salê çuyî me ve xwe bi haft (heft) dolara difrot.
 
Last year we sold it ourselves for seven dollars.

135
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:10,000
Firq(Ferq) mabêna sûncikê gûz û ya behîva çi ye? Firqa xwe
heyi lê?
 
What is the difference between walnut sucuk and almond
sucuk? Is there a difference?

136
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:14,000
Firqa xwe tenne(tune). Mesele a hayi j behiv e hez dike..
dibe a behive mi da.
 
There is no difference. For example, someone likes almond...
they say give me the almond one.

137
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Yê heyî jî, dibe gûzê mi de, tu firq(ferq) a ten ne(tune).
 
Some also say give me the walnut one, there is no
difference.

138
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Ev çûna t'ê xu çi diki? (Ev çûnana we çêdikin?)
 
Do you make these lines/shapes yourself?

139
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:24,000
De ev çûna(xêza) şeva grê(girê) didin, me çu... na vê.
 
They tie these shapes at night, we don't... go to them.

140
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:44,000
Mesele ev çuona(şêwa) ji mirove me tînin, piştî girêdin,
şixlê(karê) dest in.
 
For example, these shapes are brought to us by our
relatives, after they tie them, it's handiwork.

141
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Ev şerbete heye..
 
There is this juice..

142
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Mesela li vê derê, ew kefa em li ser digrin, dikeve vê tûrê.
Ev tûr wek ferezan(parzûn) tê. Şerbeta pak derdixe.
 
For example, here, the foam we skim off goes into this bag.
This bag acts like a filter. It extracts the pure juice.

143
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,000
Disifîne.
 
It filters it.

144
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:50,000
Disifîne wilo, dî (wê) kine çopelik (valahî).
 
It filters it like that, into the emptiness.

145
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Destên te sax bin.
 
Bless your hands.

146
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:52,000
Destên we jî sax bin.
 
Bless your hands too.

147
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:57,000
Bi rastî heta carek me yekê li gund di.. em mexzûm bû, li
ber me danî dîsa pelûl da ber.
 
Truly, once someone in the village... we were hosted, they
served us pelûl again.

148
00:14:57,000 --> 00:15:03,000
Me sernederxist me pelûl xwar, bes em nizanin ev sûncik tu
çawa çêdikî.
 
We couldn't figure it out, we ate the pelûl, but we didn't
know how you make this sucuk.

149
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Destên xwe sax bin, Xwedê emrek dirêj bide te Xalê Ehmed.
 
Bless your hands, may God grant you a long life, Uncle
Ahmed.

150
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Xwedê siheta we jî xwaş bike, înşelleh. Em perçeyek evî xwaş
bidin xwarin, dîtina we.
 
May God give you good health too, God willing. We will
kindly give you a good piece to eat for your visit.

151
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Welle me jî kêf kir ji dîtina we.
 
Well, we are also pleased to see you.

152
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Kesên nizanin tu dimsa reş jî çêdikî..
 
For those who don't know, you also make dark dimis (grape
molasses)..

153
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:38,000
Em çêdikin, dimis cem heye. Em çêdikin... ta kî... avê ev sê
çar bermîl hene.
 
We make it, I have dimis here. We make it... up to... I have
these three or four barrels.

154
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
Xalê Ehmed, ev nîv-gûz e, wek te got?
 
Uncle Ahmed, is this a half-walnut, like you said?

155
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:50,000
Ev rub (çaryek) e. Ev nîv e. Û gûzî kamil(tev) heye.
 
This is a quarter. This is a half. And there is a whole
walnut.

156
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:55,000
Gûze ku... ev wa ye, mesela... gî dirêj e(gî di rêz e). Di
dirêzê da, gî tisafî (gî tije ye)... gûz, ev ha.
 
The walnut that is... it's like this, for example... they
are all lined up. In a line, all full of... walnuts, this
one.

157
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Ev gûzî tê da pir tê. Wezn giran tê. Û behayê (bihayê) wê jî
biha dibe yê din ra(ji yê din bihatir e).
 
There are a lot of walnuts in this one. It weighs heavy. And
its price is also higher than the others.

158
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Û ev heyî...
 
And this one...

159
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,000
Yanî ev li ser teleb a(daxwaza) wê têne çêkirin lê...
 
So these are made based on the demand for them...

160
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Ser teleb e. Ewa... Hinekî ev xwestî ye.
 
Based on demand. That... Some ask for this.

161
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Hinekî ji gûzî xwestî (hinek ev gûze xwestî)... mesela, ev
tek (yek) parçe. Erê.
 
Some ask for this walnut... for example, a single piece.
Yes.

162
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Û ewa, mesela ew ev nîv-gûz e, ewa nîv-gûz e.
 
And this one, for example, this is a half-walnut, that is a
half-walnut.

163
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Ev heyî gî(gişt)... naha wextî ti (di wextê xwe de)
çêdikirin... ma naha teleb(daxwaz) çi bibe ji wê dibe. Erê.
 
We make all these... at the time... whatever the demand is
now, we make that. Yes.

164
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:28,000
Niha ku yek vî bixwaze, ev dibe. Hinek ji vî pir xwestî, yek
gûz.. û hinek ew xwestî, hinek ew xwestî.
 
Now, if one asks for this, we make this. Some ask for a lot
of it, the whole walnut.. and some ask for this, some ask
for that.

165
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:31,000
Û her tiştî.. her cureyê wê yekî jî... behayê (bihayê) xwa..
cudaye na?
 
And everything... each type of it also... has a different...
price, right?

166
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:37,000
Başqe(cuda) ye. Noka ew bi pênc sedî ye. Nîv gûz diçe bi çar
sed û pêncî. Yê din diçe bi sê sed û pêncî ye.
 
It's different. Now that one is 500. The half-walnut goes
for 450. The other one goes for 350.

167
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Her (çiqas) em dikin bên.. gûz be(zêdetir be), biha... lê..
 
The more... walnuts are in it, the price... goes up..

168
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Li.. her gûz pir bû.. Erê.
 
Yes.. the more walnuts... Yes.

169
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:48,000
Û bes hawa... xwedê bereketê têxe... rizqî we bide înşelleh.
 
And just like this... may God put blessings in it... may He
provide for you, God willing.

170
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:51,000
Ez dixwazim.. te li ser xwaşilan. Xwaşil em dibînin li vê
derê.
 
I want you to talk... about xwaşil. We see xwaşil here.

171
00:16:51,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Xwaşil... ev xwaşil jî... ma dema (me dît ku am) bi dimis
çêdikin. Dimis keland.. xwaşil, pir tehmek(tehmê) didê,
tehma hingiv jê tê (didê).
 
Xwaşil... this xwaşil too... when we make it with dimis.
Boiling the dimis.. xwaşil, gives it a lot of flavor, it
gives the taste of honey.

172
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:07,000
Û nişê genim jî zêde dike. Yanî heta nişê genim di
qewrîne... nişê genim...
 
And it also adds wheat starch. I mean until the wheat starch
is roasted... wheat starch...

173
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Naha em kî bê (ku bên).. wextî ku ti dimsa reş çêdike, tu bi
ew xwaşilê jî çêdikî.
 
Now if we say.. when you make the dark dimis, you also make
this xwaşil.

174
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:19,000
Badî(Piştî) ew dikelînin... tehmê gewir (genim) diğeyirîne
(diguhere), tehmek xweş dibe û lonî(rengê) gewir (genim) zer
berdide dorê.
 
After they boil it... the taste of the wheat changes, it
gets a good taste and the color of the wheat spreads a
yellow hue around.

175
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Wekî din tu derman... mesele, em bên, tişt tevli nabe?
 
Do you add anything else like some other ingredient... let's
say?

176
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:33,000
No. tu tişt tê nabe. Ti tişt di mistê(di dimisê) de... tu
tişt nabe. Ğêrî (ji xeynî) xweşê ti tişt tune ye... ğêrî tiş
te nabe (û tu tişt tê nabe).
 
No. nothing else is added. Nothing in the dimis... nothing
is added. Except for its own sweetness, there is nothing...
nothing else is added.

177
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:37,000
Naha bi xibret.. xibreta sed sal in, ev kar o we ji bav û
kalên xwe rakirî heta naha.
 
Now with experience... a hundred years of experience, you
have inherited this work from your ancestors until now.

178
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Tê(te) naha ekîd tu vê sûncikê hazir di... da dibînî dikana?
ê hazir.
 
Surely you now see this ready-made sucuk in... the shops?
The ready-made one.

179
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:45,000
Ew tu çi dibînî û vê sûncika te...
 
What do you see in that one and in your sucuk...

180
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Ew sûnciko xêrî (xirab) e, ewa tîcarî ye hew, tîcarî ye ha
wa.
 
That sucuk is bad, it's just commercial, just commercial.

181
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:54,000
Naha şixulê me (ev)... gî tiriyê hew kû.. şerbet tê wa, û
yanî cehfê xwa (zehmetiya wê) pir e.
 
Now in our work... this is all just pure grapes... pure
juice, and I mean its effort is a lot.

182
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:57,000
Ew ê ku hûn dîtin... ew tiştê tîcarî, ewe şixulê... me'mel
a(karxane ne) me'mel e.
 
What you saw... that commercial thing, that's the work of...
factories, they are factories.

183
00:17:57,000 --> 00:18:00,000
Me'mel ê Ezaz ê û li Haleb ê ne.
 
Factories in Azaz and in Aleppo.

184
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:01,000
Dê çi çêkirin (Ew çi çêdikin)?
 
What do they make?

185
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Em kengê (eger) biftilin... berî vê pêncî salê tu me'mela
nîn bûn (çênedibûn). Gî malan çêdibû li gundan.
 
If we go back... fifty years ago, there were no factories.
It was all made at home in the villages.

186
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:09,000
Ev sûnciko dî çû Halebê, da hat firotan.
 
This sucuk went to Aleppo to be sold.

187
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Naha jî haziran... em dibînin... l'me'mela... û aw(ew)
tiştên din çêdikin.
 
Now also the ready-mades... we see them... in factories...
and they make those other things.

188
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:19,000
Gî me'mel a va çi dikin in, ekîd tê... tê paqij nîne (wekî
wê paqij nabe)... tê ji wan ne bes...
 
What do they make in the factories, surely you... it's not
as clean as this... it's not from them but...

189
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Lê me'mel (karxane) din çêdikin, belkî em şerbetê hînin û pê
çêkin. Û şerbêtên têde jî, em nizanin... tiştek...
 
But in the factories they make it differently, maybe we
bring the juice and make it with it. And as for their juice,
we don't know... something...

190
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:31,000
Te'mê wan jî wekî kî.. em... jê dît, evî ku em çêdikin
şerbete... me nediye tişt...
 
Their taste is also like... as we have experienced, the
juice we make... we haven't seen anything like it...

191
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Bas (Lê) me'mela xwe (gelek) heye, li Ezaz ê ye, li Halebê.
 
But there are many factories in Azaz and Aleppo.

192
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Ma... î din, ti karê destî xu yî. Tu ji te (di) ra bi
kîlok... bî çi ne h o ... sa(sal) l ... ta çikî (te çi)
erzan a u ya biha ye? Xalê Ehmed?
 
But... the other thing, it is your handiwork. For you... per
kilo... for how much now... a year... is it cheap or
expensive? Uncle Ahmed?

193
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Welle tire (naha)... n w e (ne wekî) salê çûyî nê. Sale çûyî
biha bû.
 
Well now... it's not like last year. Last year it was
expensive.

194
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Ev sal erzan e. Dibe bi dev(deh) û pênco(pêncî), dev(deh) û
pênc nîvo... dev(deh) û çora(çar) nîvo... em vî salê
difroşin.
 
This year it's cheaper. It might be 10 and 50, 10 and a
half... 10 and 4 and a half... we sell it for this this
year.

195
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:55,000
Dms(Dimsa) reş... vî sal e kiloyê... bi çend e Xalo Ehmed?
 
The dark dimis... this year, a kilo... how much is it Uncle
Ahmed?

196
00:18:55,000 --> 00:19:02,000
Wil e kiloya dimis reş... am difirta(ya me difirot)... di
bên... bi şuşa em difroşin.
 
Well, a kilo of dark dimis... that we sold... they say... we
sell it by the bottle.

197
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Şîşê me difroşin. Sê kîlonî, bi şêstî ye. Kîloyê der sî(20).
(Kîlo te(tê) bi bîstî lîreyî ye).
 
We sell it in bottles. The three-kilo one is for sixty. A
kilo comes out to twenty.

198
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:10,000
Çor e dolar(çar dolar) e na. Kîlo jê tê(dibe) çar doler e.
 
That's four dollars, right? A kilo is four dollars.

199
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:17,000
